@domenic @sideshowbarker 
https://www.w3.org/TR/html5/links.html mentions `<link rel=icon href=gnome.svg sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml">` - is it outdated syntax and instead for SVG expected `<link rel=mask-icon color=… href=…>`?
Do we want to keep 2 specifications? If "yes", then why not to combine it with backwards compatibility like `<link rel=icon href=gnome.svg sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml" color="red">`? (Perhaps `sizes="any"` is unnecessary, but it is another conversation.)
